# Install with: scrontab scripts/slurm/nightly.scrontab   (view: scrontab -l; remove: scrontab -r)
# Every night at 01:30 Pacific a 1-CPU launcher (scripts/slurm/nightly_launch.sh, M2-21 decision 18;
# scrontab may not accept --array) submits the nightly job array (scripts/slurm/nightly.sbatch) on the
# latest origin/main: 0 integration + contract + nf-test, 1 benchmarks (wheat), 2 calibration_nightly,
# 3 real giap run on sim100k; then a 1-CPU afterany summary job that posts the night's results.
# Proposed for Khoa (M2-21); Khoa reinstalls it after the merge.
#SCRON --job-name=giap-nightly-launch
#SCRON --partition=normal
#SCRON --qos=normal
#SCRON --cpus-per-task=1
#SCRON --mem=1G
#SCRON --time=00:10:00
#SCRON --output=/home/classes/bios/270/khoa/giap/local/logs/giap-nightly-launch.%j.out
30 1 * * * /home/classes/bios/270/khoa/giap/scripts/slurm/nightly_launch.sh
